/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (At the same time, the ecosystem is not without challenges. Changes and revisions to subsidy policies in the past have created uncertainty and caused fluctuations in demand, making it harder for companies to plan pricing and expansion. The charging landscape is also changing. Investments in shared and open charging networks by third-party providers are increasing, reducing the need for company-owned networks like Ather Grid. While proprietary charging once acted as a strong advantage, its importance is gradually declining as more public options become available. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8 9]
