>>
endobj
300 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The sourcing process drew from both domestic and international partners who provided high-quality components for batteries, chargers, and power electronics. The company maintained stringent quality checks for every element that entered the vehicle. This focus on quality helped strengthen the brand's credibility but made cost optimisation more challenging during periods of financial strain. Additionally, the financial pressures faced by Ather extended to its suppliers. As the company expanded, it relied heavily on supplier credit and negotiated timelines to manage cash flow, placing strain on smaller component suppliers who often operated with tight margins.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A critical component of Ather's operational model was the Ather Grid, the company's proprietary fast-charging infrastructure network. Currently, it possesses the capability to charge 15 kilometres worth of range in just 10 minutes. Initially positioned as a unique advantage to reduce range anxiety for early adopters, the Ather Grid required continuous investment in installation, electricity, and maintenance.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
